{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1205615-2e-lunar-half-caste-and-moonsilver-tattoos","id":1205615,"title":"[2e] Lunar Half-Caste and Moonsilver Tattoos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-11T08:55:20-07:00","id":1205615,"title":"[2e] Lunar Half-Caste and Moonsilver Tattoos","content":"So, I'm about to begin playing in a 2e Exalted game in which the players have been encouraged to come up with the most outlandish concepts we can think of. I have settled on the idea of a Lunar Half-Caste who exalted as a Solar, but I've hit a snag. I've taken Material Resonance so I can attune to Moonsilver as if I were a Lunar, but I vaguely remember somewhere something saying that only a full Lunar could actually benefit from receiving Moonsilver tattoos. Does anybody know if this is true, and if so, where it would be located? Joining the Silver Pact is kind of an important part of his backstory and I like the symbolic gesture of having received the tattoos as if he were an actual Lunar, having gone through their entire initiation ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:04:02-07:00","id":1205639,"title":"","content":"Are half castes even accorded full or rather any membership in the silver pact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:26:28-07:00","id":1205652,"title":"","content":"If gonzo is the name of the game, just go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T02:36:36-07:00","id":1206833,"title":"","content":"1e has an explicit bit about non-Lunars being allowed to go through the trials to gain a place in Lunar society (page 62).<br /> <br /> However, in both 1e and 2e, Form-Fixing Method assumes a tattooed Lunar is tattooing an un-tattooed Lunar (rather more explicitly in 1e), and a major part of the tattoos is fixing caste. I'd be tempted to suggest your character was indeed tattooed, but without a Lunar Exaltation they're <i>just</i> tattoos rather than magically potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:23:47-07:00","id":1206938,"title":"","content":"Or maybe the tattoos have an effect that isn't EXACTLY what the Moonsilver does for a Lunar (blanket immunity to Wyld taint and a laundry list of Bad Touch mojo). It'd be cool to see more worthwhile mechanical bennies for Creation's flavorful &quot;small magics&quot;<br /> <br /> Also don't expect the term &quot;Half-Caste&quot; to come back, because it turns out that the phrase has a pretty, uh, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half-caste\" target=\"_blank\">loaded history</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T21:15:51-07:00","id":1207528,"title":"","content":"I'd let the tattoos function and skip the caste part.<br /> <br /> <b>Page 28, 2E, Lunars:</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Ironically, while Wyld inflicted the curse of shifting castes, the Wyld also held the possibility of a cure. Experimenting with moonsilver, the Wyld\u2019s tendency to turn people into living stories and strange Wyld-shaping techniques stolen from the Fair Folk, the sorcerers found a way to construct a magical identity that could withstand Wyld erosion. The process first required the Lunar to recite a list of her past accomplishments and proclaim why they should accord her status within a caste. Then, those deeds would be tattooed onto the Lunar\u2019s body with pure moonsilver, along with various magical sigils. Once the tattoos were complete, a protected Lunar\u2019s caste could resist the Wyld indefinitely. Furthermore, the Lunar also became completely immune not only to Wyld-shaping effects but to all transformative magical effects which targeted her body.&quot; </div> </div> </div>The tattoos don't rely on something inherently &quot;Lunar&quot; about your essence - they're merely an ugly work-around they invented to try fixing a splat-specific debility. <b>Anyone who frequents the Wyld </b>as often as the Silver Pact does would have reason to desire them.<br /> <br /> In essence, the tattoo is just the &quot;canon&quot; version of your life story --- so when the Wyld tries to rewrite you into one of its fanfics -- your artifact says &quot;NOPE!&quot; and laughs it off. <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Compare and contrast Alchemical charm slots. Sure, they're specific to Alchemicals - but the books had mention of Eclipses being able to dive into the vats, get implants installed, and proceed so they can acquire such charms if needed. Just because it was <i>designed for Alchemicals</i>, didn't forbid non-Alchemicals from using it.<br /> <br /> Same thing with &quot;Sidereal Martial Arts&quot; - non Sidereals learn them too.<br /> <br /> Same thing with Necromancy - non Abyssals can learn them.<br /> <br /> Same thing with various Jade-skin/limb/eye artifacts - designed for Terrestrials, but nothing inherently forbids Celestials from getting them installed.<br /> <br /> The only obstacle here is social (will the Silver Pact use a precious magical material on a Half-Caste to tattoo him). But maybe if you had several feats of heroism (including acquiring the raw moonsilver in the first place - maybe you delved into a ruin no one else had risked, etc), you'd have knocked out those concerns first.<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Edit: One issue I <b>do</b> have with the tattoos tho - what about your post-tattoo life? Are Lunars stuck in a Peter Pan-esque Never-Never-Land? The tattoos reaffirm <b>who you are narratively</b> - so while they can illustrate your loose archetype (&quot;I am a Warrior and thus a Full Moon&quot;), can they also prevent growth?<br /> <br /> What if the hypothetical Warlord-Lunar wants to become a famous Crafter or Scholar? They start a family, etc. But every time they revisit the Wyld.... those traits aren't magically etched on their skin. So they revert back to the Warlord-Lunar, who thinks &quot;bah, scholarship was a waste of time anyways&quot; or &quot;mortals are weak, I can't mourn inferior kin&quot;.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Lunars <b>do</b> update tattoos to show case debts and replayment - but <b>is that profound enough to record?</b> Must a debt be forever etched into one's skin as an important memory? Etc.<br /> <br /> (a bit of a tangent, but just part of the problem with the way this artifact seems to work)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 04-16-2018, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}